+\subsection{Explicit fixed-binary import adapters}
+
+Binary80 and binary128 name numeric formats, not stable C++ native types.
+The adapter layer therefore uses semantic wrappers parameterized by the
+consumer-selected native type:
+
+\begin{lstlisting}
+auto r80 = gmpfrxx_mkII::adapters::make_binary80_source(value80);
